# spectral-x402 — runtime secrets. Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# PUBLIC VALUES ONLY. This kernel is a key-less seller: it receives at an
# address and the facilitator performs settlement. It never signs, never
# transfers, and has no code path that wants a spending key. Startup REFUSES
# if any X402_* variable holds something shaped like a private key, a seed
# phrase, or a keystore.

# ─── Seller receiving address (PUBLIC — safe to paste, appears on-chain) ────
# Resolves the manifest's payToRef "roblox-luau-payto".
# Format: 0x followed by exactly 40 hex characters.
# The spending key for this address should live in hardware, offline, and
# never on this machine.
X402_PAYTO_ROBLOX_LUAU_PAYTO=
X402_PAYTO_MEDICAL_MEDLINEPLUS_PAYTO=
X402_PAYTO_FINTEL_PAPER_ARENA_PAYTO=

# ─── Facilitator ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base Sepolia facilitator base URL, speaking standard x402 v2. Mainnet
# (eip155:8453) stays startup-blocked until a signed manifests/mainnet-gate.json
# validates.
#
# https://x402.org/facilitator needs no API key and supports exact/eip155:84532.
# A CDP facilitator does; its key goes in X402_FACILITATOR_API_KEY and is sent as
# a bearer token on /verify, /settle and /supported.
#
# Setting this DISABLES the stub — but delete X402_ALLOW_STUB_FACILITATOR from
# .env.local anyway. Leaving it there is one edit away from free data.
X402_FACILITATOR_URL=
X402_FACILITATOR_API_KEY=

# ─── Ops surface ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ed25519 PUBLIC key (base64) authorized to sign /ops requests. The matching
# private half stays on the operator's machine and is never read here.
X402_OPS_PUBKEY_B64=

# ─── Sepolia test client (NOT the server) ───────────────────────────────────
# The buyer used to prove settlement end-to-end is the ONE place a private key
# exists in the whole flow. It belongs to a throwaway testnet wallet, it is read
# by the settlement-gate HARNESS and never by the kernel, and it lives in the
# macOS Keychain — not in this file, not in the server's environment, and NOT
# under an X402_* name (boot sweeps those and refuses to start on a key-shaped
# value, which is a guard worth keeping meaningful).
#
#   security add-generic-password -a "$USER" -s x402-payer-key -w
#   npm run gate:settlement
#
# See docs/SETTLEMENT-PROVISIONING.md.
